tterns as vertices, a customer\nadjacent to each pattern it requires, and `ω` is the largest number of customers on one\npattern. The forest hypothesis of the item's title buys only the second step: when the\nincidence graph is acyclic its components are trees on at most `n + m` vertices, so\n`TreeBound.lean`'s size bound gives `pathwidth (incidence M) ≤ tb (n + m)` with\n`tb N = ⌊log₃((6N + 3)/5)⌋`, the least `k` with `N ≤ treeBound k`.\n\nChecked before it was stated (item 06, `reports/scratch/forest_check/`): zero violations on\n4,410 record rows with both pathwidths exact, 594 depth-one block graphs and 2,000 random\ninstances, 1,799 of them not forests; and again for this file on the 3,448 forest instances\non record (`learning/sandwich.py --stage forest`, `reports/scratch/forest_cover/`).\n\n## The construction (`blowUp`)\n\nFrom a path decomposition `D` of the incidence graph, the bag `i` of the MOSP graph is\n*the customers in `D.bag i` together with the customers of every pattern in `D.bag i`*\n(`blowBag`). A pattern's customers are a clique and all enter with the pattern, so every\nedge of the MOSP graph is covered by any bag holding the pattern. The interval property is\nthe union-of-intervals lemma of §6.2: a customer `c` appears through `inl c` or through one\nof its patterns `inr p`, every one of those vertices shares a bag with `inl c` (edge coverage\nin `D`), and a union of intervals each meeting a common interval is an interval\n(`PathDecomposition.mem_bag_of_meet`, the three-way case split on the meeting bags). The bag\nhas at most `a + b·ω ≤ (a + b)·ω ≤ (width + 1)·ω` customers, where `a` customers and `b`\npatterns sit in `D.bag i`.\n\n## Main results\n\n* `incidence M : SimpleGraph (C ⊕ Pt)` — `Adj (inl c) (inr p) ↔ M.requires c p`, symmetric,\n  nothing else (`incidence_adj_inl_inr`, `incidence_adj_inr_inl`, `incidence_not_adj_inl_inl`,\n  `incidence_not_adj_inr_inr`).\n* `maxPatternSize M` — `ω`; `one_le_maxPatternSize_iff`: `1 ≤ ω ↔ ∃ c p, M.requires c p`.\n* `blowUp D : PathDecomposition M.mospGraph` with `blowUp_width_add_one_le`:\n  `(blowUp D).width + 1 ≤ (D.width + 1) · ω` when `1 ≤ ω`.\n* `pathwidth_mospGraph_add_one_le` — **(L2)** `pathwidth M.mospGraph + 1 ≤ (pathwidth (incidence M) + 1) · ω`\n  when `1 ≤ ω`; `mospValue_le_maxPatternSize_mul` — **F1 in MOSP terms, no hypothesis**:\n  `mospValue M ≤ ω · (pathwidth (incidence M) + 1)`.\n* `treeBoundInv N = Nat.log 3 ((6N + 3) / 5)` with `le_treeBound_treeBoundInv`\n  (`N ≤ treeBound (treeBoundInv N)`) and `treeBound_lt_of_lt_treeBoundInv` (it is the least\n  such `k`): Lemma 5 of §6.2 as an integer identity.\n* `pathwidth_le_treeBoundInv_of_isAcyclic` — **(L3)** every forest on `N` vertices has\n  pathwidth at most `treeBoundInv N` (per component through\n  `pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected` and `tree_pathwidth_le_treeBound`).\n* `mospValue_le_of_incidence_isAcyclic` — **(L4), F1′**:\n  `(incidence M).IsAcyclic → mospValue M ≤ ω · (treeBoundInv (|C| + |Pt|) + 1)`.\n\n## The layer lemma (item 07, Lemma L)\n\n* `IsLayering G lvl` — adjacent vertices at most one level apart; `layer lvl i` the vertices at\n  level `i`; `layerWidth lvl h = max_{i ≤ h} (|L_i| + |L_{i+1}|)`.\n====GATE\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0010 (the excess phase diagram).\n\nPasses only if all five hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every `.lean` file under lean/MOSPFormalization/ (top level, Complex/ and\n   Search/) is imported by lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really\n   checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (0: the development has none since Appendix E) plus\n   the entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes, and so does `pytest` in\n   pathwidth_solver/;\n5. the paper builds with no undefined references (`make -C paper1/latex check`).\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0010/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 0\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\nPAPER = REPO / \"paper1\" / \"latex\"\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n        out.append(src[i]); i += 1\n    return \"\".join(out)\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    ok = True\n    b = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"build\"], cwd=LEAN, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((b.stdout + b.stderr).splitlines()[-25:])\n    if b.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: lake build\\n\" + tail); return 1\n    print(\"lake build: ok\")\n\n    root = (LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        mod = \"MOSPFormalization.\" + \".\".join(f.relative_to(LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").with_suffix(\"\").parts)\n        if not re.search(rf\"^import {re.escape(mod)}\\s*$\", root, re.M):\n            print(f\"GATE FAIL: {mod} is not imported by MOSPFormalization.lean\"); ok = False\n\n    sorries, axioms = [], []\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        code = strip_comments(f.read_text())\n        for n, line in enumerate(code.splitlines(), 1):\n            if re.search(r\"\\bsorry\\b\", line):\n                sorries.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n            if re.match(r\"\\s*(private\\s+)?axiom\\b\", line):\n                axioms.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n    allowed = [l for l in ALLOWED.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith(\"#\")] if ALLOWED.exists() else []\n    limit = BASELINE_SORRIES + len(allowed)\n    print(f\"sorry in code: {len(sorries)} (limit {limit}): {sorries}\")\n    if len(sorries) > limit:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: more sorry than the baseline plus allowed_sorries.txt\"); ok = False\n    if axioms:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eaef906-d850-4c3f-88f5-ed685df4fdaf","uuid":"3a1af823-3fee-44de-bcb6-5fa1fe210605","timestamp":"2026-11-01T08:24:32.888Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/-\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n\n# Pathwidth\n\nThe pathwidth of a graph is the minimum width over all path decompositions.\n-/\n\nimport MOSPFormalization.PathDecomposition\nimport Mathlib.Order.Lattice.Nat\n\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization\n\nvariable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V)\n\n/-- The pathwidth of a graph: minimum width over all path decompositions. -/\nnoncomputable def pathwidth : ℕ :=\n  sInf (Set.range (fun P : PathDecomposition G => P.width))\n\n/-- Pathwidth is at most the width of any specific decomposition. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_width (P : PathDecomposition G) :\n    pathwidth G ≤ P.width := by\n  apply Nat.sInf_le\n  exact ⟨P, rfl⟩\n\n/-- Pathwidth is at most `Fintype.card V - 1` (trivial decomposition). -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_card_sub_one :\n    pathwidth G ≤ Fintype.card V - 1 := by\n  calc pathwidth G ≤ (PathDecomposition.trivial G).width := pathwidth_le_width G _\n    _ = Fintype.card V - 1 := PathDecomposition.trivial_width G\n\nend MOSPFormalization\n====HELLY\n75-pa