ntifier `le_or_lt`\nerror: MOSPFormalization/PendantCliques.lean:177:84: Tactic `rcases` failed: `x✝ : ?m.261` is not an inductive datatype\nSome required targets logged failures:\n- MOSPFormalization.PendantCliques\nerror: build failed\n\nreal\t0m1.296s\nuser\t0m1.039s\nsys\t0m0.467s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/MOSPFormalization/PendantCliques.lean","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":247,"lines":["+/-","+Copyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.","+Released under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.","+","+# The two-sided pendant bound (Lemma P)","+","+Item 06 of `reports/excess_phase_plan.md` (`reports/excess_phase_diagram.md` §6, Lemma P)","+proved on paper, for every graph `G` with a clique `R` and cliques `Q_1, …, Q_q` of size at","+least `t` that meet `R` in exactly one vertex each, at distinct vertices `v_1, …, v_q`, that","+","+  `pathwidth G ≥ t + ⌈q/2⌉ − 2`.","+","+It is a pathwidth argument that is not degree-based: the clique floor `ω − 1` sees only one","+clique, the pendant bound sees how `q` cliques hang off one. On random small graphs it is","+above the clique floor on a few per cent (`reports/scratch/pendant_cliques/check.log`), and","+on item 03's block-graph families it is exact at depth one (Theorem F2 of §6, whose lower","+half it is). This file is item 13 of loop0010 (the reserve), the next Lean target §6.5 named","+(L5).","+","+Checked before it was stated: 1,905 random graphs on 2–8 vertices with exact pathwidth, every","+clique as `R`, every choice of pendant cliques dominated — zero violations, tight on 1,474","+(`reports/scratch/pendant_cliques/check.py`); and item 06's 594 depth-one graphs and 2,000","+random instances before that.","+","+## The proof","+","+Let `X_0, …, X_L` be a path decomposition. By the Helly property","+(`PathDecomposition.exists_bag_of_isClique`) `R` lies in some bag `X_a` and each `Q_i` in some","+bag `X_{b i}`.","+","+* If some `b i = a`, the bag `X_a` holds `R ∪ Q_i`, which has `|R| + |Q_i| − 1 ≥ q + t − 1`","+  vertices (`v` is injective into `R`).","+* Otherwise every `b i` is strictly left or strictly right of `a`, and one side holds at least","+  `⌈q/2⌉` of them. On the left, let `j` have the largest `b j`: for every other `i` on that","+  side, `v_i` lies in `X_{b i}` and in `X_a` with `b i ≤ b j ≤ a`, so in `X_{b j}` by the","+  interval property; and `v_i ∉ Q_j` because `Q_j ∩ R = {v_j}` and `v_i ≠ v_j`. So `X_{b j}`","+  holds `Q_j` and `⌈q/2⌉ − 1` further vertices: at least `t + ⌈q/2⌉ − 1`. The right side is","+  the mirror image (`j` with the smallest `b j`).","+","+Either way some bag has at least `t + ⌈q/2⌉ − 1` vertices, so the width is at least","+`t + ⌈q/2⌉ − 2`. In `ℕ`, `⌈q/2⌉ = (q + 1) / 2` and the statement is","+`t + (q + 1) / 2 ≤ pathwidth G + 2`.","+","+## Main results","+","+* `PathDecomposition.pendant_bound` — the bound for one decomposition,","+  `t + (q + 1) / 2 ≤ D.width + 2`.","+* `pathwidth_ge_of_pendant_cliques` — **(L5), Lemma P**: `t + (q + 1) / 2 ≤ pathwidth G + 2`.","+* `MOSPInstance.mospValue_ge_of_pendant_patterns` — in MOSP terms: a pattern `p₀` and `q`","+  patterns `p i` with at least `t` customers each, meeting `p₀` in exactly one customer `v i`,","+  the `v i` distinct, force `t + (q + 1) / 2 ≤ mospValue M + 1`.","+* `pathwidth_ge_of_clique_pendant_cliques` — the depth-one case `t = q = s` behind","+  `CT(s, 1, b) = ⌈3s/2⌉ − 2`: a clique of size `s` with a clique of size `≥ s` pendant at each","+  vertex forces `s + (s + 1) / 2 ≤ pathwidth G + 2`.","+-/","+","+import MOSPFormalization.MOSPGraph","+","+set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false","+","+namespace MOSPFormalization","+","+variable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {G : SimpleGraph V}","+","+/-! ### Three facts about `Q ∩ R = {x}` -/","+","+theorem mem_left_of_inter_eq_singleton {Q R : Finset V} {x : V} (h 