{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DgfgtR7BB1Cr4k5DjP63mG","type":"tool_result","content":"                 wall: float | None = None) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Every candidate on every certified instance, resumable by\n    `(instance_name, source)`, largest instances first.\"\"\"\n    from learning.conjecture import _generated_matrix\n    from learning.extremal import matrix_key\n\n    rows = certified_rows()\n    rows = rows[rows[\"source\"].isin(sources)]\n    done: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()\n    if out_csv.exists():\n        prev = pd.read_csv(out_csv)\n        done = set(zip(prev[\"instance_name\"], prev[\"source\"]))\n    todo = rows[[(a, b) not in done for a, b in zip(rows[\"instance_name\"], rows[\"source\"])]]\n    if limit is not None:\n        todo = todo.sort_values(\"n_customers\", ascending=False).head(limit)\n    print(f\"[harness] {len(rows)} certified rows, {len(done)} done, {len(todo)} to run\", flush=True)\n    matrices = corpus_matrices(todo) if (todo[\"source\"] == \"corpus\").any() else {}\n    jobs = []\n    for r in todo.sort_values(\"n_customers\", ascending=False).itertuples():\n        if r.source == \"corpus\":\n            mat = matrices.get(r.instance_name)\n            if mat is None:\n                continue\n        else:\n            mat = _generated_matrix(r)\n        jobs.append((r.instance_name, r.source, matrix_key(mat), names))\n    started = time.monotonic()\n    part: list[dict] = []\n    written = 0\n    with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=workers) as pool:\n        futures = [pool.submit(_validity_job, j) for j in jobs]\n        try:\n            for i, fut in enumerate(as_completed(futures), start=1):\n                part.append(fut.result())\n                if len(part) >= 500 or i == len(futures):\n                    _append(out_csv, pd.DataFrame(part))\n                    written += len(part)\n                    part = []\n                    print(f\"[harness] validity {i}/{len(futures)} in {time.monotonic() - started:.0f}s\",\n                          flush=True)\n                if wall is not None and time.monotonic() - started > wall:\n                    print(\"[harness] wall reached; cancelling the rest\", flush=True)\n                    for f in futures:\n                        f.cancel()\n                    break\n        finally:\n            if part:\n                _append(out_csv, pd.DataFrame(part))\n    return load_values(out_csv)\n\n\ndef _append(csv: Path, part: pd.DataFrame) -> None:\n====CONJ\nsolutions\n427:def all_rows() -> pd.DataFrame:\n578:def load_table(inv_csv: Path = INVARIANTS_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n====TEX\nshare of instances whose $B$ is a forest falls from $0.74$--$0.92$ below\n$e_g(r)$ to $0.23$--$0.40$ between $e_g(r)$ and $1$, and is zero above\n(measured). Figure~\\ref{fig:excess} places every instance of\nSection~\\ref{sec:results} against the three. Below $e_g(r)$ the open stacks\nare governed by the largest pattern (Theorem~\\ref{thm:blowup}); between\n$e_g(r)$ and $1$ the first moment says nothing and the deterministic bounds\nare all there is; between $1$ and the ridge the certified optimum per\ncustomer sits $0.02$--$0.10$ above $\\beta^{*}$ and the cost of certification\nclimbs, and this is where the $d=2$ classes of Section~\\ref{sec:results}\n($e=1.66$--$1.78$) and 22 of the 24 industrial instances sit; above the ridge\nthe cost falls and $\\beta^{*}$ comes within $0.04$--$0.06$ of the certified\nslope at $e\\ge6$ ($m=n$, 30--100 customers), the $d=4$ classes\n($e=2.9$--$3.7$) being the dense shoulder. No benchmark instance we hold has\n$e<e_g(r)$, and 12 of $6{,}376$ have $e<1$.\n\n\\paragraph{The forest regime.}\nWrite $\\omega$ for the size of the largest pattern.\n\\begin{theorem}[blow-up]\n\\label{thm:blowup}\nFor every instance, $\\mathrm{MOSP}\\le\\omega\\,(\\pw(B)+1)$. If $B$ is a forest,\n$\\mathrm{MOSP}\\le\\omega\\bigl(\\lfloor\\log_{3}\\tfrac{6(n+m)+3}{5}\\rfloor+1\\bigr)$.\n\\end{theorem}\nReplace each pattern node in each bag of a path decomposition of $B$ by the\npattern's customers: a customer's nodes in $B$ form a star, so its bags stay\nan interval, and no bag grows by more than a factor $\\omega$. Nothing about\n$B$ is used; the forest enters only through the pathwidth of a forest on $N$\nvertices, at most $\\lfloor\\log_{3}((6N+3)/5)\\rfloor$, which is sharp. Both are\nLean theorems~\\leanref{blowup}~\\leanref{forest}. The bound is loose: on 7,004\ngraphs with exact pathwidth (clique trees to 936 vertices, random block trees,\n3,448 certified random covers whose $B$ is a forest, and 2,000 small random\ninstances) it is never violated and never exact, 2 to 5.5 times the truth on\nthe block-graph families; on the 3,448 random forests the pathwidth is\n$\\omega-1$ on $99.8\\%$, so below $e_g(r)$ the optimum is, in practice, the\nlargest pattern (measured). The exact theory on block graphs is polynomial\n\\citep{ChouKoHoChen2008}; on clique trees the exact values grow by about\n$(\\omega-2)/2$ per level of depth, no formula linear in $\\omega$ and the depth\nfits them, and we conjecture no closed form.\n\n\\paragraph{Constructions from above.}\n\\begin{lemma}[layers]\n\\label{lem:layer}\nIf $L_0,L_1,\\dots$ are the distance layers from any vertex of a connected\ngraph, $\\pw\\le\\max_i(|L_i|+|L_{i+1}|)-1$; and $\\pw\\le n-\\alpha$ for any\nindependent set of $\\alpha$ vertices.\n\\end{lemma}\nThe bags are $L_i\\cup L_{i+1}$, and $(V\\setminus I)\\cup\\{v\\}$ for $v\\in\nI$~\\leanref{layer}~\\leanref{indep}. On the uniform cover model with $m=\\mu n$\npatterns of size $d$ the layer sizes follow a two-type exploration recursion\nand the greedy independent set that takes the customer with fewest patterns\nfollows a differential equation; the smaller limit is a constant\n$\\beta^{+}(d,\\mu)$, derived on paper up to the concentration step, which we\ncite and do not re-prove. Table~\\ref{tab:excess} gives it beside $\\beta^{*}$\nand the slope $b$ of $\\mathrm{opt}=a+bn$ on the certified instances at\n30--100 customers. The sandwich\n$\\beta^{*}\\le\\liminf\\mathrm{opt}/n\\le\\limsup\\mathrm{opt}/n\\le\\beta^{+}$ has\nwidth below $0.12$ at $e\\ge14$ and $0.42$--$0.49$ for $1\\le e\\le3.5$: it says\n====CHECKLEAN\n28:def cited() -> set[str]:\n30:    for f in sorted(HERE.glob(\"sec*.tex\")):\n41:    files = {p: p.read_text() for p in LEAN.rglob(\"*.lean\")}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eaef906-d850-4c3f-88f5-ed685df4fdaf","uuid":"cc81a279-f863-4f39-8a32-836b450fb121","timestamp":"2026-11-01T08:31:01.028Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"                 wall: float | None = None) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Every candidate on every certified instance, resumable by\n    `(instance_name, source)`, largest instances first.\"\"\"\n    from learning.conjecture import _generated_matrix\n    from learning.extremal import matrix_key\n\n    rows = certified_rows()\n    rows = rows[rows[\"source\"].isin(sources)]\n    done: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()\n    if out_csv.exists():\n        prev = pd.read_csv(out_csv)\n        done = set(zip(prev[\"instance_name\"], prev[\"source\"]))\n    todo = rows[[(a, b) not in done for a, b in zip(rows[\"instance_name\"], rows[\"source\"])]]\n    if limit is not None:\n        todo = todo.sort_values(\"n_customers\", ascending=False).head(limit)\n    print(f\"[harness] {len(rows)} certified rows, {len(done)} done, {len(todo)} to run\", flush=True)\n    matrices = corpus_matrices(todo) if (todo[\"source\"] == \"corpus\").any() else {}\n    jobs = []\n    for r in todo.sort_values(\"n_customers\", ascending=False).itertuples():\n        if r.source == \"corpus\":\n            mat = matrices.get(r.instance_name)\n            if mat is None:\n                continue\n        else:\n            mat = _generated_matrix(r)\n        jobs.append((r.instance_name, r.source, matrix_key(mat), names))\n    started = time.monotonic()\n    part: list[dic