pendant}, and with\n$t=q=|R|$ it gives the exact value $\\lceil 3s/2\\rceil-2$ of a clique $K_s$\nwith a pendant $K_s$ at every vertex, the depth-one clique tree; with the\nmatching decomposition (on paper), $K_s$ with a pendant $K_t$ at $q$ of its\nvertices has pathwidth exactly $\\max(s-1,\\,t+\\lceil q/2\\rceil-2)$. It is a\npathwidth argument that is not degree-based, and on the certified instances\nit is worth little: evaluated over the maximal cliques of the MOSP graph it is\nabove the clique floor $\\omega-1$ on 554 of the $6{,}376$ and tight on\n$44\\%$, but above the solver's bound on 5, and above $\\max(\\text{solver\nbound},\\,\\mathrm{tw}+1)$ on 3 of the 338 instances where that bound misses by\ntwo or more, by one stack each (measured, 9--134 customers).'''\ns=s.replace(anchor,add)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnice -n 19 python -m pytest tests/test_pendant_cliques.py -q -x 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Add the Appendix A row and the Appendix E lemma, rerun the tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":199829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":812,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eaef906-d850-4c3f-88f5-ed685df4fdaf","uuid":"660a52d8-0cb1-4088-a96b-91b6baeef29c","timestamp":"2026-11-01T08:34:24.667Z","request_id":"req_011CgbuAbQUdXY6cQNrd5PNd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01U1ir7y7U53FpsTjxoeuSD3":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='paper1/latex/sec9a_appendix_lean.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=r'''\\leanentry{indep}{Lemma~\\ref{lem:layer}, the independent-set bound $\\pw\\le n-\\alpha$, by the bags $(V\\setminus I)\\cup\\{v\\}$} \\leannames{pathwidth_le_card_sub_indepN