ss's `max(lb_best, tw + 1)` with `tw` the exact or interval","+treewidth of the invariants table, as §14 (3) asked.","+","+**6,376 of 6,376 scored, 19 s wall on 8 workers, 0.03 core-hours, 172","+censored evaluations (all caps, none a deadline): 0 violations** (no value","+above a certified optimum — the Python agrees with the theorem on every","+instance); **tight on 2,809 (44.1%); above the clique floor `ω − 1` on 554;","+above the solver's `lb_best` on 5; above `max(lb_best, tw + 1)` on 5**. On the","+**338 bound-gap instances**: above `ω − 1` on 89, above the reference on","+**3**, by **one stack each**, tight on 0:","+","+| instance | n | optimum | lb_best | tw + 1 | reference | Lemma P |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| Warwick 871: balanced orders, 4 orders per product | 20 | 6 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 5 |","+| p1540n9_0 (Faggioli–Bentivoglio) | 40 | 7 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 6 |","+| p1550n8_0 (Faggioli–Bentivoglio) | 50 | 8 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 7 |","+","+By collection (all corpus rows; `mean gap` is `optimum − lb_best`, `mean P","+gap` is `optimum − Lemma P`):","+","+| collection | instances | tight | above ω − 1 | above lb_best | above reference | mean gap | mean P gap | censored | median s | max s |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| Harvey | 2,130 | 690 | 381 | 1 | 1 | 0.28 | 3.08 | 61 | 0.000 | 0.56 |","+| Challenge | 46 | 14 | 5 | 0 | 0 | 0.91 | 4.59 | 1 | 0.001 | 0.03 |","+| Chu & Stuckey | 200 | 0 | 77 | 0 | 0 | 5.43 | 26.3 | 97 | 0.039 | 3.89 |","+| Faggioli–Bentivoglio | 300 | 68 | 44 | 3 | 3 | 1.02 | 3.25 | 0 | 0.000 | 0.002 |","+| SCOOP | 24 | 5 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1.04 | 1.25 | 0 | 0.000 | 0.001 |","+| Miller | 1 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0.00 | 7.00 | 0 | 0.000 | 0.000 |","+| Shaw | 25 | 0 | 4 | 0 | 0 | 0.44 | 4.96 | 0 | 0.001 | 0.002 |","+| Simonis | 3,630 | 2,018 | 41 | 0 | 0 | 0.18 | 1.34 | 12 | 0.000 | 0.64 |","+| Wilson | 20 | 14 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1.55 | 4.00 | 1 | 0.001 | 0.03 |","+","+By size band:","+","+| customers | instances | tight | above ω − 1 | above lb_best | above reference | mean gap | mean P gap | censored |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| ≤ 20 | 4,122 | 2,253 | 160 | 2 | 2 | 0.13 | 1.07 | 0 |","+| 21–30 | 1,816 | 471 | 296 | 0 | 0 | 0.45 | 4.10 | 61 |","+| 31–40 | 197 | 56 | 26 | 2 | 2 | 0.82 | 5.27 | 24 |","+| 41–50 | 120 | 21 | 28 | 1 | 1 | 1.66 | 8.98 | 30 |","+| 51–75 | 31 | 0 | 15 | 0 | 0 | 4.32 | 26.6 | 15 |","+| 76–100 | 63 | 8 | 18 | 0 | 0 | 8.78 | 30.0 | 27 |","+| 101–134 | 27 | 0 | 11 | 0 | 0 | 13.3 | 53.0 | 15 |","+","+The bound-gap instances by collection: Harvey 71 (above `ω − 1` 36, above the","+reference 1), Challenge 3 (0, 0), Chu & Stuckey 102 (34, 0), Faggioli–Bentivoglio","+83 (18, 2), SCOOP 3 (0, 0), Simonis 73 (1, 0), Wilson 3 (0, 0).","+","+### 16.4 Findings","+","+1. **Lemma P is a theorem for every graph, in Lean, in the form the paper","+   cites** (Lemma \"pendant cliques\" of Appendix E, row `pendant` of Appendix","+   A), with its MOSP form and the depth-one case that explains item 03's","+   `CT(s, 1, b) = ⌈3s/2⌉ − 2` from below. F2's upper half stays on paper.","+2. **It is worth little on the record.** It beats the clique floor on 8.7% of","+   the corpus and on 26% of the bound-gap instances, but the solver's bound","+   (contraction degeneracy, in the main) already sees what it sees: above","+   `lb_best` on 5 of 6,376, above `max(lb_best, tw + 1)` on 3 of the 338 gap","+   instances, by one stack, never on a Chu & Stuckey instance. §14 (3) is","+   answered: not worth anything there.","+3. **Where it bites is depth one.** On the three instances it helps, the","+   MOSP graph has a clique with large cliques hanging off several of its","+   vertices and little else; on the gap instances of `ml_nature.md` §6 —","+   trees of cliques *with branching below the first level* — the pendants","+   are themselves branched, and Lemma P sees only the first level. The","+   branch lemma family (§38) and F3's recursion see deeper and were closed","+   by the harness already; a bound for the gap instances needs an argument","+   that is neither the clique floor, nor degree, nor one level of pendants.","+4. **The evaluation's caps bind only on dense instances** (172 censored, 97","+   of them Chu & Stuckey, where the maximal-clique count exceeds 5,000);","+   lifting the caps could only raise those values, and on the dense","+   instances the bound is 26–53 stacks short, so the verdict does not depend","+   on them.","+","+### 16.5 Kill verdict","+","+The item carries none. For §14 (3), the natural criterion — Lemma P beats","+the reference on some bound-gap instance by two or more stacks, or on more","+than a handful — is **not met** (3 instances, one stack each): the bound","+idea is closed on this record, as the branching family was in §38.","+","+### 16.6 What this does not claim","+","+- **Not the exact optimum of Lemma P over all clique pairs.** The evaluation","+  takes `R` and the pendants among maximal cliques (and the cut-down","+  sub-cliques of the pendants); a sub-clique of a maximal clique as `R` can","+  do better in principle. On the 1,905 small graphs of 16.1, where every","+  clique was tried, the maximal-clique evaluation agrees with the exhaustive","+  one on every graph in the test module's 120-graph sample; above that it is","+  a lower bound on the lemma's best value, hence still a valid bound.","+- **Not a statement about generated instances or the ensembles**: the corpus","+  only, 9–134 customers.","+- **Not F2 in Lean.** The upper half (the three-part decomposition of §6.2)","+  is on paper and checked by the DP on 72 graphs; Lean has the lower half","+  only.","+- **Not a solver change.** `pendant_graph_bound` is not called by","+  `_lower_bound`, and on this record it would change 5 starting points by one","+  stack."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/excess_phase_diagram.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013FNMjx5me6cgFraregFABv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept",